+# aims Guide State
+
+Loop status only. Not the design record.
+
+## Mode
+
+auto
+
+## Loop cursor
+
+ready-to-choose-next
+
+## Current objective
+
+**Kind:** add-feature
+
+**Objective:** The effective timeout of any request sent through a Session is decided by exactly one owner,
+which applies the session's configured default on every path through the session and yields to an explicit
+per-call timeout.
+
+**Why now:** PO change: set a default timeout once per Session; calls that forget `timeout=` must not hang.
+PO handed the None-semantics choice back ("choose a simple, sensible approach"): chosen — per-call `None`
+counts as "not passed" (session default applies); explicit no-limit per call is the existing `(None, None)`
+/ urllib3 `Timeout(None, None)`.
+
+**Exit criteria:**
+- [x] Session with default D; `s.get(url)` (no timeout kw) → adapter receives D. Same for every verb method and `s.request`.
+- [x] `s.get(url, timeout=None)` → adapter receives D (falsifier: a `setdefault("timeout", ...)` shortcut fails this, because `request()` always passes `timeout=None` explicitly).
+- [x] `s.get(url, timeout=T)` for float T, tuple, urllib3 Timeout → adapter receives T unchanged; no field-wise mixing of tuples with D.
+- [x] `s.get(url, timeout=(None, None))` with default D → no limit reaches the adapter (explicit opt-out survives).
+- [x] `s.send(prepared)` directly, no timeout → D applies.
+- [x] Redirect chain (2+ hops) → every hop's adapter call gets the same effective timeout as the first.
+- [x] Response hooks receive the resolved (effective) timeout in their kwargs.
+- [x] End to end: default 0.x s on a slow endpoint raises ReadTimeout without any per-call timeout.
+- [x] No default configured → adapter receives exactly what was passed (None when omitted) — characterization.
+- [x] Pickle round-trip keeps the default; unpickling a state from before this change (no timeout key) works and means "no default".
+- [x] Invalid default (e.g. 3-tuple) fails with the same ValueError as an invalid per-call value.
+
+**Preserve:**
+- Session with no default: bit-for-bit current behavior; module-level `requests.get` etc. unchanged.
+- Existing TestTimeout tests pass unedited (4 connect-timeout tests fail environmentally, as before).
+
+**Do not optimize for:**
+- A general "session settings" framework, a new sentinel type, validation machinery foreign to Session's plain-attribute grain.
+
+## Worker handoff (drafted — do not execute before the build command)
+
+ROLE: implementation Worker; the design is the deliverable.
+DESIGN GOAL: one owner for "effective timeout" across all send paths of a Session; the change lands at the
+existing seam, matching Session's grain (plain public attributes like `stream`/`verify`/`cert`).
+BEHAVIOR: the exit criteria above.
+WHAT GOOD AIMS AT: design-principles.md + add-feature-principles.md (characterize first; one owner; re-trace
+the interactions: redirects, hooks, Response.next, pickling).
+TESTING: test-first; characterization of no-default behavior before touching code; every criterion a test.
+PRESERVE / NON-GOALS: as above. Module/placement choices are the Worker's.
+RETURN: code + tests + design reasoning; met | partially_met | invalidated | blocked.
+
+## Open assumptions (unproven — carried, not filed)
+
+- "Every request made through that session" includes direct `Session.send()` and redirect hops (grounded reading of PO text).
+
+## Open Guide TODO
+
+- [x] None-semantics decision — handed back by PO; chosen as above; filed in src/requests/sessions.py.md (anchored).
+- [x] Prove the default applies through every send path (tests: verbs, request, send, Response.next, redirects, hooks).
+- [x] Prove no-default sessions are unchanged (characterization tests passed before and after; full suite unedited).
+
+## Last evaluated result
+
+met — 35 new tests pass; full suite 650 passed, only the 4 known environmental connect-timeout failures; setdefault-shortcut mutation caught by 18 tests. Pyright not installed in .venv, not run.
