 -------------------
diff --git a/docs/user/advanced.rst b/docs/user/advanced.rst
index f5209a5..2927b3d 100644
--- a/docs/user/advanced.rst
+++ b/docs/user/advanced.rst
@@ -1120,6 +1120,24 @@ coffee.
 
     r = requests.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)
 
+To avoid repeating the timeout on every call, set a default on a
+:class:`Session <requests.Session>`. Every request sent through that session
+uses it unless the call passes its own timeout, which replaces the default
+entirely (a tuple is never combined field by field with the default)::
+
+    s = requests.Session()
+    s.timeout = (3.05, 27)
+
+    s.get('https://github.com')              # uses (3.05, 27)
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=5)   # uses 5
+
+On a session with a default, ``timeout=None`` means "not given" and the
+default still applies, so code that forwards ``timeout=None`` from its own
+arguments cannot turn the default off by accident. To wait forever on a single
+call anyway, say so explicitly::
+
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=(None, None))
+
 .. note:: The connect timeout applies to each connection attempt to an IP address.
           If multiple addresses exist for a domain name, the underlying ``urllib3`` will
           try each address sequentially until one successfully connects.
